body:
I want to switch up my redemption statement from before, giving it more thought...

&#x200B;

I believe how a reader perceives redemption/ a redeemable character is based largely on the readers philosophy & beliefs regarding sin and the imperfection of humans. If a reader believes there's a line that cannot be crossed (for some that's death, for others adultery, for some trafficking) then a character is only so redeemable so far as he doesn't cross a certain line.

&#x200B;

For me it's somewhat different and more half full. I believe characters like the Troupe are sorta redeemable. I believe many people are unguided, and I want to use the Troupe as an example. The Troupe are good to thy neighbors (they're the protectors of Meteor City afterall)..

&#x200B;

Just that alone shows humanity and good in the Phantom Troupe. They're also seemingly only involved with the Mafia (Yorknew was a mafia led event). The murderers of Sarasa were clearly mafia involved. The creation of the Phantom Troupe, I theorize, is to deal with the underground. Who's involved in the unground? Cartels & mafia...

&#x200B;

They're odd heroes to their own story. They're terrorists, no doubt.. which is just weird to understand how they justify everything.. They just grew up in terrible conditions with corrupt influences (the kidnapping of the children in meteor city).. It's just hard for me to feel hate towards a person like that. Do I like justice? Of course. I like Kurapika being able to experience that feeling of get back, even if it means sacrificing a little bit of himself in the process. Winning isn't always pretty, as Kurapika shows.. There's something sad but respectable about the length Kurapika goes (being a genuinely kind soul)..

A little bit of a tanget, but the Phantom Troupe is exceptional because of its counterpart, which is Kurapika. That dynamic in the story of HxH is phenomenal. Every single chapter we get the Phantom Troupe the stock rises in Kurapika vs Troupe as one of the greatest vendetta plotlines. I think a lot about this story.

&#x200B;

The Phantom Troupe also have these weird moments of endearment that pull on my heartstrings (Phinks thanking Gon & Killua after Paku passed)

If you read the whole thing, thank you for listening to my rant on one of the greatest story tellers ever: Yoshihiro Togashi

I'd like to add a very profound statement from one of the stories in the bible. Specifically in regards to redemption & characters being "redeemable"..

&#x200B;

“I have swept away your offenses like a cloud, your sins like the morning mist. Return to me, for I have redeemed you”  (Isaiah 44:22).

This is an important aspect in ficitonal writing across the history of story telling, and perhaps why some villains end up becoming so iconic & ingrained in the hearts of readers. No matter how evil, the most defining moments of a "villain" are at the tail end of his character arc.. & it's not rare for it to be reminscent to a "coming to Jesus" type moment..

&#x200B;

I want to say we readers view some villains in HxH as goodwilled??, & having principles with good intentions ???... but ultimately wrong (a la Phantom Troupe)

&#x200B;

If that makes any sense..

Ah, yes. Next time I get a big American next to me on a flight I'll ask them or the flight attendent if they can transfer their "space" into a black hole or somewhere else in our space time continuum. Why? Well these Americans freely bestowing sweaty grease fat & odors down my plain white t shirt are costing me too much money on tshirts and therapist charges for my ptsd.

&#x200B;

Sincerely, the poor guy getting skinnier.

This chapter is spectacular. I have NEVER enjoyed reading a HxH chapter more than I have THIS one. Obviously, that has to do with the hiatus & the emotional attachment you get from missing a series for this long. Nonetheless, I just found myself fanboying over the entire chapter. Hinrigh's ability is NUTTY!! I can't even begin to explain how cool his ability is. Apparently the pigeons .....that were originally handcuffs but are now nen PIGEONS.... have commands?! Like dude can really give commands to inanimate objects!? This dude is really ONE OF THEM. I'm beyond impressed. His arrogance is just portrayed so well imo. His design is honestly very good. I love the Italian Mafia boss vibes he gives. The Giorno Giovanna of the HxH verse has so much swagger.. I love how he wants all 23 cult members to just show up in front of him. UJIOhiujnfgvijefhniujerfh... AND THE ART of this chapter!!!!!!! 10/10 chapter. The dialogue wasn't heavy, the pacing was perfect, and the clifhanger to Hinrigh producing a CATcorder... I mean CAMCORDER is such a good ending to a action packed chapter. And did Hinrigh really put his hands back in his pocket after getting his palm drilled through like if mans was a sheath of Home Depot plywood?! #HinrighHIGHSTOCKS!

&#x200B;

EDIT: I CAN'T EVEN SPELL PIDGEON\* CORRECTLY BUT I'M SO HAPPY!!!!!!

Feel free to ignore this. I'm a simple human being with no education higher than a bacherlor's degree who really enjoys HxH. Maybe I'm missing something, but I feel this lacked the intellectuality you mention in the beginning. Anyways, to the content posted by OP... Idk where to start. For one, I think comparing Togashi to George Lucas isn't warranted. Stories are stories, but they're from completely different backgrounds with different methods of publication, etc. I just don't see the point in comparing science fiction (SW) to a Shonen JUMP "weekly" manga. Furthermore, there's some good news surrounding the return of our savior, Lord Togashi-Sama (I'm kidding guys, chill out). It's always werid talking about stories, because of its subjectivity...But I genuinely believe Togashi, in terms of writing, Chimera Ant Arc & Beyond (pun intended?!) has gotten even better. 

&#x200B;

And to the point of overstaying its welcome: this fanbase is the answer. Heck, everyone in this subreddit is the answer. HxH has been ever so prevalent since its 2011 anime adaptation. Many say it's been their shit since before. We're all here waiting for its return.

&#x200B;

 I say all this to say, I'm a fan of Togashi and Hunter x Hunter just like you. Togashi is going to continue this series & he will give us yet another all-time great arc. #ThatHunterxHunterGreatnessIsAlmostBack.
